<title>GERMANY: RWE says 96/97 profit, sales up.</title>
<headline>RWE says 96/97 profit, sales up.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fiscal year to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales				  70,800  vs 65,400</p>
<p>    --energy				     21,100  vs 21,400</p>
<p>    --mining and raw materials	     4,000   vs 4,800</p>
<p>    --oil and chemicals			26,900  vs 24,200</p>
<p>    (of which petrol tax)		    10,600  vs 10,500</p>
<p>    --waste management			 1,700   vs 1,300</p>
<p>    --engineering and plant construction 8,600   vs 7,300</p>
<p>    --construction			     7,400   vs 5,900</p>
<p>    --telecommunications		     1,100   vs 500</p>
<p>    Investments				  10,700  vs 7,200</p>
<p>    Cash flow				    9,000   vs 8,700</p>
<p>    Workforce (headcount)		    133,473 vs 132,648</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German energy group is RWE AG. The company said its net profit excluding minority interests rose by seven percent to just under 1.3 billion marks. Excluding acquisitions, group sales rose four percent. The workforce declined by 5.4 percent on a comparable basis.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
